AssetCollectionManifestV1.description:
Framework-owned zero-to-many media relation. The generated child table is
still an ordinary SQLite table for OCC, backup, and live-query purposes;
this descriptor is the exclusive authority to mutate it.
@ref LLP 0239#d2-assetcollection-is-the-zero-to-many-application-relation

AssetCollectionOperationV1.description:
Closed operation vocabulary carried by generated collection mutations.
Application handlers cannot construct this plan through the public IR.
@ref LLP 0239#d2-assetcollection-is-the-zero-to-many-application-relation

video.description:
@ref LLP 0044#video-location-policy-the-video--location--sibling-block-dated-decision-2026-08-03 —
video location policy has its own manifest carrier rather than
overloading or aliasing the frozen image-policy spelling.

ConfigEntryDefinition.description:
@ref LLP 0036#declared-configuration-in-the-manifest — one declared config
entry: names, purposes, and acquisition metadata are app source (public by
construction); values never appear in any manifest.

permissionBacking.description:
Durable row-existence projection that grants the room permission in
sessions mode. The subject field equals the connection-bound user id;
every mapped table field equals its named room-scope field.

limitRejections.description:
Operations rejected by a hard room/store limit (L9). Structured
rejection, never silent eviction.

@ref LLP 0026#limits-and-diagnostics — limits are capability facts.

oneOf.description:
`v.vector(dimensions)` — an exact fixed-dimension binary64 vector.
Ordinary arrays keep their separate 1,024-item contract ceiling.

@ref LLP 0132#the-vvectordimensions-value

uses.description:
@ref LLP 0036#declared-configuration-in-the-manifest — D8: the config
entries this function may receive. Declaring an entry makes it exist;
only functions that name it here are granted it at runtime.

GeneratedAuthorityOperationKindV1.description:
Closed identity of an authority-profile operation synthesized by codegen.
This is a manifest fact emitted from a module-private generator marker;
function names and declared dependencies alone never grant this identity.

HostedAuthCapabilities.description:
Closed hosted-auth capability descriptor authored by the serving target.

@ref LLP 0060#d5-hosted-readiness-is-conjunctive — every deployment fact
and the browser credential posture is independent and fail-closed.

MediaFieldDescriptorV1.description:
Semantic facts for the finalized-only member of the AssetRef family.
The application column still contains only the opaque asset id.
@ref LLP 0244#d1-one-authoritative-media-result-materialization-cut

oneOf.description:
One point-shaped host allocation. It is legal only inside a validated
`write-with-activity.v1` plan, after the exact scope owner guard.
@ref LLP 0135#12-allocation-surfaces

joinedTableVisibility.description:
The exact restricted joined-table policy. Storage composes it with
`joined_visibility`, so a row must satisfy both predicates.

@ref LLP 0231#d3--composed-into-the-plan-sized-by-a-plan-class-model

rootTableVisibility.description:
The exact restricted table policy derived from the installed schema.
Public-read is normalized to absence, matching `QueryPlan`.

@ref LLP 0231#d3--composed-into-the-plan-sized-by-a-plan-class-model

liveLimits.description:
Optional lower ceilings for the separately capability-gated live
search surface. Absence selects the target's admitted defaults.

@ref LLP 0136#capability-id-and-claim-discipline-llp-0119-oq2-proposal

VectorIndexManifestV1.description:
The complete table-local identity of one exact vector index.

@ref LLP 0132#vector-values-and-declarations — one version binds the vector
  field, dimensions, metric, release policy, ordering, and every work bound.
